---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { contactEmail, legalUpdated, siteName } from '../lib/site';
---

<InfoLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Timezone Prime"
  description="How Timezone Prime handles your data: no accounts, no ads, no tracking cookies. Settings stay in your browser and conversions run on your device."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  lead="The short version: we do not track you, we do not sell anything about you, and your conversions never leave your device."
  crumb="Privacy policy"
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  updated={legalUpdated}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information {siteName} (timezoneprime.com, "we", "us") handles when you use the website,
    and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we do not collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not ask you to create an account or give us your name.</li>
    <li>We do not use analytics, advertising or social media trackers.</li>
    <li>We do not set cookies.</li>
    <li>
      The times, dates and zones you enter are converted inside your browser. They are not sent to us or stored on any
      server.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Settings stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    To remember your preferences between visits, the site saves two small values in your browser's local storage. They
    stay on your device and are never sent to us.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>tzp:theme</code> remembers whether you chose the light or dark colours.</li>
    <li><code>tzp:hour12</code> remembers whether you prefer a 12 or 24 hour clock.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can remove them at any time by clearing this site's data in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>Your time zone</h2>
  <p>
    The converter reads your device's time zone setting so it can start from your local time. This happens in your
    browser and the value is not sent to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like almost every website, our hosting provider automatically records basic technical details when a page is
    requested, such as IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time of the request. These logs are used to
    keep the site secure and running, are kept for a limited period, and are not used to identify or profile you.
  </p>

  <h2>When you email us</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact us, we receive your email address and whatever you include in your message. We use it only to reply
    and to fix any problem you report. We do not add you to a mailing list or share your message with anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages link to other websites, such as the source of our map data. Those sites have their own privacy policies,
    and we are not responsible for how they handle your information.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is a general-purpose tool and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, laws such as the GDPR or CCPA may give you the right to access, correct or delete
    personal information we hold about you. In practice the only personal information we may hold is an email you sent
    us. To ask about it or have it deleted, write to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how the site handles information, we will update this page and the date at the top. If we ever add
    analytics or advertising, this policy will say so before it goes live.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy can go to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> or through the
    <a href="/contact/" data-astro-reload>contact page</a>.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
